  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Fine sand and crystal-clear water at the far end of Pampelonne bay, with a view of Cap Camarat. Escalet has a nice touch that's rare on this stretch of coast: a dog shower installed right on the beach, to rinse the sand and salt from your dog's coat after swimming.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>As on the rest of Ramatuelle's beaches, dogs on leash are allowed outside the supervised swimming areas. The presence of a dog shower makes it one of the most practical beaches in the area for wrapping up the day without bringing all the sand back home.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: arrive early in the morning, before the car park fills up — late morning is the busiest time in summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The coastal path links Escalet to Cap Camarat and its lighthouse — a lovely way to extend a walk with your dog after swimming.</p>
    </div>

    <aside>
